  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member writing a long reply with the modern composer, I want the card to stop growing once it reaches its maximum height (about 12 lines at text size 100 %) and scroll its text inside, so that it never slides behind the keyboard.\n\n### Observed (operator, 2026-11-20, device, `dev-swift` build, Réglages › Taille du texte 100 %)\n- The docked card grows correctly with each new line up to about **12 lines** (the #1136 behaviour, #1223).\n- Past that point, new lines keep growing the card, **not only upwards but downwards too**: its bottom slides **behind the keyboard**.\n- Expected: at that height the card **freezes**; further lines scroll inside the editor.\n\n### Source\n- #1223 (`ced6568d`, #1136): « the docked card grows with the reply up to the room the screen leaves », with `ComposerKeyboardRoom` (no room until the keyboard has shown once; a hidden keyboard keeps the last room). The cap is reached (~12 lines) but not enforced as a hard maximum on the card's frame, or the card's bottom is not pinned to the keyboard's top once the cap is reached.\n- Same area as #1285 (card behind the keyboard after a smiley is inserted): one fix may cover both; keep two issues so each acceptance criterion is checked.\n\n### Scope\n- The card's height is `min(content height, room left above the keyboard)`; its bottom stays pinned to the keyboard's top (or the safe area when the keyboard is down) at every height; past the maximum, the editor scrolls and keeps the caret visible.\n- The maximum follows the text size (about 12 lines at 100 %, fewer lines at larger sizes: it is a height, the room the screen leaves, not a line count).\n- No change to the legacy composer.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- Typing lines past the maximum: the card height stays constant, its bottom never goes below the keyboard's top, the caret stays visible.\n- iPhone and iPad, portrait and landscape, text size 100 % and one larger size.\n- A test that fails without the fix (the pure height/room model: content taller than the room → height equals the room, bottom anchored).\n- Device check listed on #893.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
