   "updated_at": "2026-11-22T22:09:10Z",
   "body": "Analysis from a cloud session (read of `dev-swift` @ `0e8bb39`, no device).\n\n**Read**\n- Pure model: once the cap binds, `cardHeight == availableHeight` (`textCap` takes the buttons, chips, controls, insets and `editorInsets` off the room), so the text-only symptom is not in the model.\n- The docked card is a `safeAreaInset(.bottom)` of the reader: its bottom is placed by SwiftUI's keyboard safe area. A bottom that slides behind the keyboard looks like lost keyboard avoidance, as in #1285. Suspect, not a conclusion.\n- **One real defect found**: `ReplyComposerView.editorCard` uses `measured.editorHeight`, but `measured.chips` is only set on the detent's copy (`ReplyComposerView.swift:316`). With an inserted image the cap ignores the chips row, so the card is one chips row too tall for the room. A separate PR fixes that (`Refs #1286`); the text-only symptom stays open here.\n\n**A Mac session must reproduce and capture** (text only, no image): simulator, modern composer on, text size 100 %, type 13+ lines. Read at 11, 12, 13 and 14 lines: the bar's frame in window coordinates, the keyboard frame, the bar's and the reader's `safeAreaInsets.bottom`, `layout.availableHeight`, `cardHeight`, `editorHeight`. Does the bottom move at the line where the cap binds? Repeat with a larger text size.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
