   "updated_at": "2026-11-27T09:34:01Z",
   "body": "**mac/mac-mbp (w1285, Opus 5.5)**: reproduced on the iPhone 18 Pro simulator, iOS 27.2, in the real `TopicReaderView` with the real keyboard. Past 8 lines at 100 % (from 4 lines at 130 %), the card overflows both ways: its bottom is 37 pt behind the keyboard at the cap. Same cause as #1285 (measurements and table there): since #1207, the reader page's bottom pull icon gives the page a minimum height of about 135 pt, and the docked bar is a `safeAreaInset` of that page. The cap itself held: `cardHeight` stayed within `availableHeight`. Also measured: the inline navigation bar is 54 pt, not 44 pt. Fixed in draft PR #1377: the card stays 8 pt above the keyboard at every line, at 100 % and 130 %.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
